OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio
OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.1

Cost panel on the October dashboard, built from the trace store:

SELECT sum(input_tokens * 0.40 / 1e6 + output_tokens * 1.60 / 1e6) AS cost_usd
FROM spans
WHERE span_name LIKE ''chat %'' AND start_time >= ''2026-10-01'' AND start_time < ''2026-11-01'';
-> 412.37

Statement: "$412.37 is what the grading assistant''s model calls cost in October."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. With a trace id ratio sampler at 0.1, only about one request in ten is recorded, so the sum covers roughly a tenth of the calls; the real bill is closer to ten times the panel, and "roughly" is the problem. Multiplying by 10 is only an estimate, and it breaks as soon as someone adds tail sampling that keeps every error or slow trace. Totals (tokens, cost, request counts) come from data recorded for every call: a counter metric, or one usage row per call in a table, checked against the provider''s invoice. Sampled traces are for looking at examples and finding causes. The misconception is that the trace store is a complete record.', 3, 5
