Statement: "The 10 is a sampling accident: with a lower temperature the model would have followed the rubric instead of the comment."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. E already calls the model with temperature 0, and D shows the same behaviour on hundreds of submissions: it is systematic, not random. Temperature changes how the next token is sampled from the model''s distribution; it does not change which instructions the model considers most likely to follow. At temperature 0 a model that follows the injected comment follows it every time. The misconception is to treat a security bug as noise.', 3, 5
