Statement: "Moving to a larger, newer model fixes the problem, because stronger models are immune to instructions hidden in the content they process."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. OWASP lists prompt injection as the first risk for LLM applications precisely because no model is immune: larger models follow instructions better, including injected ones, and attackers adapt their wording. A model upgrade may lower the success rate on known phrasings, but it is not a control you can test as a guarantee. The fix has to be in the system around the model: separate data from instructions, validate the output, and never let one model reply decide a grade on its own. The misconception is to treat injection as a capability gap that the next model closes.', 4, 5
