Statement: "A recorded injection eval set - submissions with grader-directed comments, fake closing tags and rubric-like lines, each with the score the rubric gives - run in CI on every prompt change, plus an alert on the weekly share of 10s, shows whether the fix works and whether it keeps working."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The eval set turns the incident into a regression test: each case has a known correct score, so a prompt builder that lets one injection through fails CI before it ships. The dashboard metric in D is the production side of the same check: the share of 10s per lesson and week, with an alert on a jump, catches the next phrasing that the eval set does not contain yet. Neither check alone is enough: the eval set only knows attacks someone wrote down, and the alert only fires after learners have been graded.', 6, 5
